/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - No column is perfectly straight.
   - The initial bow is not a defect to ignore.
   - For a sine-shaped bow of mid-span size a, the exact mid-span moment is Pa/(1 − P/PE).
   - Take a pinned strut of length L, bending stiffness EI, and load P applied with eccentricity e at both ends.
   - E is Young's modulus (Pa), I is the second moment of area (m⁴), v is sideways deflection (m), P is axial compression (N), e is load eccentricity or equivalent initial bow (m), and x is distance along the strut (m).
   - σmax is the peak compressive stress (Pa), P is axial load (N), A is cross-section area (m²), e is load eccentricity or equivalent bow (m), c is distance from centroid to extreme fibre (m), r = √(I/A) is radius of gyration (m), Le is effecti
   - The factor sec((π/2)√(P/PE)) multiplies the primary moment P e, so it is the moment magnification factor.
   - Design checks use σmax.
   - Perry-Robertson is the same idea written as an empirical column curve.
   - The secant formula is elastic.
*/
