/* book: lead: Euler's formula assumes the material is linear elastic all the way to buckling. That holds only while the stress is below the proportional limit. On a short or intermediate aircraft strut the stress can pass this limit first, and the material is then softer: its tangent stiffness Et is less than Young's modulus E. The column buckles below the Euler load. This chapter gives the tangent-modulus and  */
