/* book exam traps: Using Euler when λ < λp: Euler gives a stress above the proportional limit and is invalid. | Quoting Kármán's Er as the modulus that starts the buckle. Shanley's result is that Et starts it; Er is an upper bound. | Mixing L in metres with r in millimetres. Convert both to the same unit before computing λ. | Using σy in place of σprop to find λp for Euler validity. The proportional limit is the correct cut-off. | Applying Johnson above λJ. The parabola is only valid up to λJ; above it use Euler. */
